# plans/archive/INOUT_LOCAL_BINDINGS_AUDIT.md §9 H5: an `inout(name) := place` local
# binding inside an `io.async` body is REJECTED (v1). A state machine addresses
# a local both as `sm->var_x` and as a per-state C copy, so an alias could read
# a stale copy after a write through the reference. Since Phase 4.1 the
# evaluator rejects it (E0904), so `check` reports it too; this case pins the
# whole-program compile.
stdout_keep_match=error\[E0904\]|is not supported inside an 'io.async' body that awaits yet
timeout=120
